  "pr_title": "build(tooling): add the guide image renderer to scripts",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nAnyone on the team can render the animations in `docs/guide.md` again when the plugin or the CLI changes. Before this change, the renderer was only on one local machine.\n\n## Summary\n\n`scripts/guide_images/` renders each guide step from a scene in `scenes/`. A scene is a TypeScript script of actions, such as \"open the command palette\" or \"show this notice\". Each frame is a pure function of time, so `render.py` seeks to each frame and takes a screenshot in headless Chromium. Pillow then writes `docs/images/<scene>.gif` and a static PNG of the last frame. The `--still` option writes single frames for a check of a scene.\n\nChromium cannot run TypeScript. The page loads from a `.invalid` host name, and a Playwright route serves each file from the folder. Node strips the types from each `.ts` file with `module.stripTypeScriptTypes` before the page receives the file, so the renderer needs no bundler. `tsconfig.json` sets `erasableSyntaxOnly` and `verbatimModuleSyntax`, so the scenes use only syntax that type stripping can remove.\n\nThe shared code has one responsibility for each module: `motion.ts` (easing curves), `state.ts` (frame state and the sample content), `script.ts` (timeline steps), `views.ts` (app windows), and `scene.ts` (the runner).\n\nPlaywright and Pillow are in a new `guide` dependency group. The default `uv sync` does not install them. A ty override ignores missing imports in `scripts/guide_images/`, so `ty check` passes when the group is not installed. A new pre-commit hook type-checks the scenes with the plugin's `tsc` when they change.\n\n`CONTRIBUTING.md` describes how to install the group and Chromium, render scenes, keep scene text in sync with `obsidian-plugin/main.ts` and `src/spsync/`, and use only sample content. `CODING_STANDARDS.md` and `AGENTS.md` list the new folder.\n\nThe committed images do not change. This change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe pre-commit hook passed: ruff format, ruff check, ty, anti-slop-python, pytest, and the new `guide-images` type check. `lefthook validate` passed.\n\nI rendered all nine scenes with `render.py`. The last frame of each scene is identical, pixel for pixel, to the committed PNG in `docs/images/`. The new GIFs are about 0.26 seconds shorter than the committed GIFs, because the renderer no longer adds an empty outro. This PR does not update the committed GIFs.\n\nManual check: run the commands in the \"Guide images\" section of `CONTRIBUTING.md` on a clean clone.\n\n## Issue\n\nRefs #13\n"
}